; Regression: under PLIRON_X16=1 a borrowed address scratch is saved in
; the 16 bytes below `sp`, so an `sp`-based access needs `off + 16` to
; fit imm12. A `SlotOffset` in (4079, 4095] (fits un-bumped, overflows
; bumped) used to hit `expect("the bump is small and aligned")` in
; `mem_finalize` — the compress_to_vec_inner / brotli ICE. With the fix
; the mode takes the `mov` + RegReg form instead. Run:
;   PLIRON_X16=1 clif-check codegen tests/x16/clif out.json
function u0:0(i8x16) apple_aarch64 {
    ss0 = explicit_slot 8192, align = 16
    sig0 = (i64) apple_aarch64
    fn0 = colocated u0:1 sig0

block0(v0: i8x16):
    v1 = stack_addr.i64 ss0
    store.i8x16 notrap v0, v1+4088
    call fn0(v1)
    return
}
